/surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Application of a stochastic passing-name calculus to representation and simulation of molecular processes</article-title><source>Inf Proc Lett</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>31</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b007"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Regev</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Silverman</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Shapiro</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Representation and simulation of biochemical processes using the <italic>&#x003c0;-</italic>calculus process algebra</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Pacific Symposium on Biocomputing (PSB2001)</source><conf-date>3&#x02013;7 January 2001;</conf-date><publisher-loc>Big Island, Hawaii, United States</publisher-loc><fpage>459</fpage><lpage>470</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b008"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Degano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldari</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Causal &#x003c0;-calculus for biochemical modeling</article-title><source>Lect Notes Comput Sci</source><volume>2003</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>33</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b009"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Degano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Priami</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldari</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Modeling biochemical pathways through enhanced <italic>&#x003c0;-</italic>calculus</article-title><source>Theor Comput Sci</source><volume>325</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>140</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b010"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Milner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Parrow</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>A calculus of mobile processes (i and ii)</article-title><source>Information Computation</source><volume>100</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>72</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b011"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Degano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Priami</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Enhanced Operational Semantics: A tool for describing and analysing concurrent systems</article-title><source>ACM Comput Surveys</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>135</fpage><lpage>176</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b012"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hucka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Finney</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauro</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolouri</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyle</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The systems biology markup language (sbml): A medium for representation and exchange of biochemical models</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>524</fpage><lpage>531</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12611808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b013"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Paun</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Membrane computing</article-title><source>An introduction</source><publisher-loc>Berlin</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Springer-Verlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b014"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reddy</surname><given-names>VN</given-names></name><name><surname>Mavrovouniotis</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Liebman</surname><given-names>MN</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Petri Net representations in metabolic pathways. In: Proceedings of the Fourteenth International Conference on Intelligent Systems in Molecular Biology; July 1993; Bethesda, Maryland, United States. Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence</article-title><source>ISMB</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>328</fpage><lpage>336</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7584354</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b015"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prandi</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Priami</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Quaglia</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Process calculi in a biological context</article-title><source>Bull EATCS</source><volume>85</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>69</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b016"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiarugi</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Curti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Degano</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Marangoni</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>ViCe: A VIrtual CEll</article-title><source>Lect Notes Comput Sci</source><volume>3082</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>220</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi-0030174-b017"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wandrey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchholz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Takors</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Quantification of intracellular metabolites in <named-content content-type="genus-species">Escherichia coli</named-content> k12 using liquid chromatographic-electrospray ionization tandem mass spectrometric techniques</article-title><source>Anal Biochem</source><volume>295</volume><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11488613</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="n102" fn-type="previously-at"><p>A previous version of this article appeared as an Early Online Release on July 26, 2007 (doi:<ext-link ext-link-type="doi" xlink:href="10.1371/journal.pcbi.0030174.eor">10.1371/journal.pcbi.0030174.eor</ext-link>).</p></fn><fn id="ack2" fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding.</bold> This work has been carried on within the PRIN project BISCA. PD has been supported by EU-IST project 016004 SENSORIA and the Microsoft Research&#x02013;Trento University Centre for Computational and Systems Biology. RM has been also supported by Italian MIUR grant Italy&#x02013;Israel FIRB &#x0201c;Pattern Discovery Algorithms in Discrete Structures, with Applications to Bioinformatics.&#x0201d;</p></fn><fn id="ack3" fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing interests.</bold> The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>